{
  "case_id": "2010-09-5801",
  "document_hash": "3582b5486727c8536ee8e3ad37b52fa12ec3eefc8ad1d60d3ce22db130f7c813",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-09-5801",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3582b5486727c8536ee8e3ad37b52fa12ec3eefc8ad1d60d3ce22db130f7c813",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3582b5486727-0000-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In Nguyen, the Court approved the imposition of legitimation requirement only upon fathers of non-marital children born abroad. That was based on biological differences between men and women."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2010-09-5801",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3582b5486727c8536ee8e3ad37b52fa12ec3eefc8ad1d60d3ce22db130f7c813",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3582b5486727-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But here, the residential requirements that are at issue here have no biological basis. They set up barriers to the transmission of citizenship by younger fathers, but not younger mothers, and they are based upon gender stereotypes that women, not men, would care -- would care for non-marital children."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-09-5801",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3582b5486727c8536ee8e3ad37b52fa12ec3eefc8ad1d60d3ce22db130f7c813",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3582b5486727-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: What separates a stereotype from a reality? Do you say it is not true that if there is a legitimate -- illegitimate child, it is much more likely that the woman will end up caring for it than that the father would?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondent",
      "case_id": "2010-09-5801",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3582b5486727c8536ee8e3ad37b52fa12ec3eefc8ad1d60d3ce22db130f7c813",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3582b5486727-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "that Congress was concerned about statelessness, but the record doesn't support that claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2010-09-5801",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3582b5486727c8536ee8e3ad37b52fa12ec3eefc8ad1d60d3ce22db130f7c813",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3582b5486727-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: No, he would have a remedy. The remedy for an equal protection violation is to treat everybody the same."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Hubachek",
      "case_id": "2010-09-5801",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "3582b5486727c8536ee8e3ad37b52fa12ec3eefc8ad1d60d3ce22db130f7c813",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3582b5486727-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "So the prospective relief notion really doesn't makes any sense in this context, because the equal protection violations have basically all already occurred at the time that the person who would make a citizenship claim was born, and we would still be left in a situation where Petitioner's father would say that I was unable to transmit citizenship to my son and a woman who was similarly situated was able to. So that type of remedy is unavailable.\nIn the Court's decision in Iowa v. Bennett, the bank case, they actually ordered a refund of the taxes that were collected in a discriminatory manner dating back in time. So if you could factor out -- if you could make a relief that would take away the benefit that others had received, then I would agree that that is available, but that's not possible in this situation.\nJUSTICE GINSBURG: Mr. Hubachek, I think the Chief asked you: If it's an equal protection violation, then the Court just says it violates equal protection, but whether it goes up or down, the Court has to give a temporary solution, because the legislature can't be convened on the spot. And the Court actually did go through that exercise, extension versus invalidation, most conspicuously in Califano -- Westcott, in the"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2010-09-5801",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "3582b5486727c8536ee8e3ad37b52fa12ec3eefc8ad1d60d3ce22db130f7c813",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3582b5486727-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Unless he's a United States citizen."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2010-09-5801",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "3582b5486727c8536ee8e3ad37b52fa12ec3eefc8ad1d60d3ce22db130f7c813",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3582b5486727-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Mr. Kneedler, if -- if the classification then were that we want to encourage, because it's good for society, father/child relationships, so we are going to give that advantage, that is 1 year for fathers, and we're going to put the mothers together with the married couples, would that be compatible with equal protection?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
      "case_id": "2010-09-5801",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3582b5486727c8536ee8e3ad37b52fa12ec3eefc8ad1d60d3ce22db130f7c813",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3582b5486727-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "All right. So, if it's tough then and really is meant to be tough, then there is a -- what is the rationale for treating women in this respect worse than treating men?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2010-09-5801",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3582b5486727c8536ee8e3ad37b52fa12ec3eefc8ad1d60d3ce22db130f7c813",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3582b5486727-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress -- Congress selected, because while I said the mothers are like the two-citizen family or two-citizen parents in the sense that only U.S. citizens are the parent and you have some connection, Congress was balancing the duration of that connection or taking into account the duration of that connection and it chose to make it a little bit tougher."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice ROBERTS",
      "case_id": "2010-09-5801",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3582b5486727c8536ee8e3ad37b52fa12ec3eefc8ad1d60d3ce22db130f7c813",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3582b5486727-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 48,
        "start": 48
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Counsel, if we determine that the only remedy we can impose is to equalize up -- in other words, add to the burden on the mother rather than relieving the father of it, do you have authority for the proposition that we can address that issue hypothetically?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2010-09-5801",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "3582b5486727c8536ee8e3ad37b52fa12ec3eefc8ad1d60d3ce22db130f7c813",
      "evidence_id": "ev-3582b5486727-0002-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 12:06 p.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    },
